ry":null,"compliance":{"score":117,"max":216,"pct":54,"assessed":"2026-02-25","notes":"Technically competent, commissioner-overseen TMSS: the core prudential indicators are all present with figures - strongest on capital expenditure/CFR (full year-on-year CFR bridge), the borrowing strategy (clear internal-borrowing/under-borrowing narrative), a properly constructed four-balance liability benchmark chart, the MRP policy statement, and a robust creditworthiness policy using CDS beyond ratings. Weakest area is commercial/non-treasury investment disclosure relative to the size of the legacy 0.9bn book: proportionality is acknowledged but not demonstrated (COM-03 core), the new commercial-income-to-net-revenue indicator is absent (PI-08), and IMPs, the paras 51-53 compliance statement, a quantitative portfolio-risk indicator, an ESG policy, separate HRA/GF benchmarks and an audit-qualification flag are all missing. Overall a compliant recovery-phase strategy whose gaps cluster in the commercial-investment and secondary-disclosure requirements.","gaps":[{"id":"PI-08","evidence":""},{"id":"LB-04","evidence":""},{"id":"COM-02","evidence":""},{"id":"COM-03","evidence":"TMSS s4.4/4.10: 0.9bn commercial initiative caused the intervention and is 'unaffordable in the long term'; being divested"},{"id":"COM-04","evidence":"TMSS s16.1-16.2: treasury (financial) investments dealt with in the TMSS, non-financial/service/commercial in the capital strategy"},{"id":"COM-05","evidence":""}],"documents":[{"title":"Annual Treasury Management Strategy 2026/27 (Council, 25 Feb 2026)","url":"https://thurrock.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s51765/Annual%20Treasury%20Management%20Strategy%20202627%20260204%20Final%20Council.pdf","fy":"2026/27"},{"title":"Final Capital Programme 2026/27-2028/29 (cover report, Council 25 Feb 2026)","url":"https://thurrock.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s51782/Capital%20Programme%2026-27%20to%2028-29%20for%20Council%2025.02.2026%20Final.pdf","fy":"2026/27"},{"title":"Appe